paraphrase.text:
Let $k \in \mathbb{Z}^+$. Show that for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $n \ge k+1$, there exists a collection of convex sets $\mathcal{C} = \{C_1, C_2, \dots, C_n\}$ and a convex set $K$ such that for any index set $I \subseteq \{1, \dots, n\}$:
\begin{itemize}
    \item If $|I| = k$, then $K \setminus \left( \bigcup_{i \in I} C_i \right) \neq \emptyset$.
    \item If $|I| = k+1$, then $K \subseteq \bigcup_{i \in I} C_i$.
\end{itemize}

exact.text:
Consider the quadratic expressions $P(t) = 2(t+2)(t-1)$ and $Q(t) = t^2 - t + 2$. Identify all $t \in \mathbb{R}$ that simultaneously satisfy:
1. $P(t) = n \cdot Q(t)$ for some $n \in \{1, 2, 3, \dots \}$;
2. $\sqrt{P(t)} + \sqrt{Q(t)} \ge \sqrt{2}$.

paraphrase.text:
Let $p(t) = 2(t-1)(t+2)$ and $q(t) = t^2 - t + 2$. Determine the set of all $t \in \mathbb{R}$ satisfying:
\ni) $p(t) = k \cdot q(t)$ for some $k \in \{1, 2, 3, \dots \}$;
\nii) $\sqrt{p(t)} + \sqrt{q(t)} - \sqrt{2} \ge 0$.

style.text:
Let $P(t) = 2t^2+2t-4$ and $Q(t) = t^2-t+2$. Determine all real $t$ satisfying both of the following conditions:
\ni) $P(t) = k Q(t)$ for some $k \in \{1, 2, 3, \dots\}$;
\nii) $\sqrt{P(t)} + \sqrt{Q(t)} \ge \sqrt{2}$.

exact.text:
Consider a graph $G$ with $N$ vertices partitioned into $M$ disjoint sets $V_1, V_2, \dots, V_M$ (countries), where $|V_i| \ge 3$ for all $i$. Let $E_{int}$ be the set of edges within sets and $E_{ext}$ be the set of edges between different sets. Suppose:
(i) $\forall i, \forall v \in V_i, \text{deg}_{V_i}(v) \ge \frac{|V_i|}{2}$;
(ii) Each vertex is incident to exactly one edge in $E_{ext}$;
(iii) For any $i \neq j$, there are at most 2 edges in $E_{ext}$ connecting $V_i$ and $V_j$;
(iv) If $|V_i| + |V_j| < 2M$, then there is at least one edge between $V_i$ and $V_j$ in $E_{ext}$.
Show that $G$ contains a simple cycle of length $L \ge M + \frac{N}{2}$.

paraphrase.text:
Seja $S$ o conjunto de números inteiros positivos que podem ser gerados a partir de $n_0 = 1$ através de uma sequência finita de transformações. Uma transformação de $x$ é definida como $2x$ ou qualquer permutação dos algarismos de $x$ na base $10$. Verifique se os seguintes valores pertencem a $S$:
\ni) $1000$;
\nii) $10^9$;
\niii) $\sum_{k=0}^9 k \cdot 10^k$.

exact.text:
Let $a, b, c \in \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$ satisfy $a \ge b$. Demonstrate that the following inequality holds:
$$\na^3 + c^3 + 1 \ge b^3 + 6(a - b)\sqrt{abc}
$$

paraphrase.text:
Determine the set of natural numbers $k$ satisfying each of the following conditions separately:
\begin{itemize}
    \item[i)] For every prime $q > 2$, the system of congruences $k^m \equiv m \pmod{q}$ and $k^{m+1} \equiv m+1 \pmod{q}$ has a solution in $\mathbb{Z}^+$.
    \item[ii)] For every prime $q > 2$, there exists $m \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $q \mid (k^m - m^2)$ and $q \mid (k^{m+1} - (m+1)^2)$.
\end{itemize}

style.text:
Let $k \in \{1, 2\}$. Determine all $x \in \mathbb{Z}^+$ such that for every odd prime $q$, there is some $m \in \mathbb{Z}^+$ satisfying the simultaneous congruences:
$$\nx^m \equiv m^k \pmod{q} \quad \text{and} \quad x^{m+1} \equiv (m+1)^k \pmod{q}
$$

exact.text:
Let $\mathcal{C}: \mathbb{N} \to \{1, 2, \dots, k\}$ be a partition of the natural numbers into $k$ sets $A_1, A_2, \dots, A_k$. Determine the minimum $k$ such that there exists a map $g: \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ satisfying:
(1) if $x, y \in A_j$ for some $j \in \{1, \dots, k\}$, then $g(x+y) = g(x) + g(y)$;
(2) $g$ is not a linear function of the form $g(n) = cn$.

paraphrase.text:
Let $S = \{1, 2, 3, \dots\}$. Determine the minimum number of cells $k$ in a partition $S = C_1 \cup C_2 \cup \dots \cup C_k$ such that there exists a map $\phi: S \to S$ satisfying:
(1) $\phi(x+y) = \phi(x) + \phi(y)$ whenever $x$ and $y$ belong to the same cell $C_i$;
(2) the set $\{x, y \in S : \phi(x+y) \neq \phi(x) + \phi(y)\}$ is non-empty.

exact.text:
Determine todos los números reales $t$ para los cuales se cumple la relación: $$
\sqrt[3]{1729-t} = 19 - \sqrt[3]{t}
$$

Let $f: \mathbb{Z} 	o \mathbb{Z}$ be a function such that $f(n) 
eq n$ for all $n \in \mathbb{Z}$. Define a set $S \subseteq \mathbb{Z}$ such that for each $s \in S$, the identity $f(x) = f(s - x)$ holds for all $x \in \mathbb{Z}$. Determine the existence of such a function $f$ for the following choices of $S$:
i. $S = \{2k + 1001, 2k + 1003\}$ where $k=0$;
ii. $S = \{1000, 1003, 1008\}$;
iii. $S = \{1002, 1004, 1006\}$.

paraphrase.text:
Let $f: \mathbb{Z} 	o \mathbb{Z}$ satisfy $f(n) 
eq n$ for all $n \in \mathbb{Z}$. Define the set $S$ of 'symmetries' such that $s \in S$ if and only if $f(x) = f(s - x)$ for all $x \in \mathbb{Z}$. Determine if it is possible for $S$ to contain the following subsets:
a. $\{1001, 1003\}$;
b. $\{1000, 1003, 1008\}$;
c. $\{1002, 1004, 1006\}$.

style.text:
Let $f: \mathbb{Z} 	o \mathbb{Z}$ be a function such that $f(n) 
eq n$ for all $n \in \mathbb{Z}$. A constant $k$ is called 'symmetric' if $f(x) = f(k-x)$ for all $x \in \mathbb{Z}$. Determine if it is possible for the set of symmetric constants to contain:
a. $\{2021, 2023\}$;
b. $\{2020, 2023, 2028\}$;
c. $\{2022, 2024, 2026\}$.

paraphrase.text:
Let $S(n)$ and $P(n)$ denote the sum and product of the decimal digits of a positive integer $n$, respectively. Determine if the following sets are non-empty:
\begin{itemize}
    \item[i.] $\{n \in \mathbb{Z}^+ : S(n) - P(n) = 10^2\}$
    \item[ii.] $\{n \in \mathbb{Z}^+ : P(n) - S(n) = 10^2\}$
    \item[iii.] $\{n \in \mathbb{Z}^+ : P(n) / S(n) = 10^2\}$
\end{itemize}

exact.text:
Déterminer les couples $(x, y) \in \mathbb{R}^2$ satisfaisant le système :
$$
\begin{cases} 
\text{arcsinh}(x) + \text{arcsinh}(y) = 0 \\ \nx^2 y^2 + x^3 + y^3 + 2x^2 + 2y^2 + 5xy + 4x + 4y + 4 = 8 
\end{cases}
$$

paraphrase.text:
Déterminer l'ensemble des couples $(a, b) \in \mathbb{R}^2$ satisfaisant le système :
\begin{cases} 
\left(\sqrt{a^2+1} + a\right)\left(\sqrt{b^2+1} + b\right) = 1 \\ 
(a^2+b+2)(b^2+a+2) = 8 
\end{cases}

exact.text:
Determine all ordered triples $(a, b, c) \in \mathbb{R}^3$ satisfying the cyclic system of equations:
$$
\begin{aligned}\na &= \frac{c^2 + 1}{b^2 + 1} \\\nb &= \frac{a^2 + 1}{c^2 + 1} \\\nc &= \frac{b^2 + 1}{a^2 + 1}
\end{aligned}
$$

