paraphrase.text:
Determine all mappings $\phi: \mathbb{Q}[t] \setminus \{0\} \to \mathbb{R}$ satisfying the following conditions for all non-zero $A, B \in \mathbb{Q}[t]$:
(1) $\phi(A \circ B) = \phi(B \circ A)$;
(2) $\phi(A \cdot B) = \phi(A) + \phi(B)$.

style.text:
Let $\mathcal{P}$ denote the set of all polynomials with rational coefficients. Determine all maps $\phi: \mathcal{P} \setminus \{0\} \to \mathbb{R}$ such that for any two non-zero elements $A, B \in \mathcal{P}$, the following conditions hold:
(a) $\phi(A \circ B) = \phi(B \circ A)$;
(b) $\phi(A \cdot B) = \phi(A) + \phi(B)$.

